menu "Tab5 on-device UI"

    config MQJS_TAB5_UI
        bool "Enable Tab5 on-device UI (MIPI-DSI + LVGL)"
        default n
        depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32P4
        help
            Drive the M5Stack Tab5 5" 1280x720 MIPI-DSI panel (ILI9881C)
            with LVGL: status bar, JS console, and (later) ui.* drawing
            bindings. Off by default so Stamp-P4 builds are unaffected;
            when disabled ui_tab5.h provides no-op inline stubs.

    config MQJS_UI_GEOM_PROBE
        bool "Geometry probe for the landscape PPA rotate hang (E2)"
        default n
        depends on MQJS_TAB5_UI
        help
            Diagnostic only. Adds ui_tab5_geom_probe(): on the UI task it
            invalidates a transparent top-layer object of fixed sizes
            (1280x28, 1280x7, 1137x8, 1138x7, 1137x7, 1137x31) one at a
            time and forces a refresh, logging GEOM_PROBE lines. In
            landscape each size becomes one PPA SRM rotate of exactly
            that chunk geometry, so the step that never prints "done"
            names the geometry that hangs. Triggered explicitly from the
            native editor with Ctrl+G (dock). Nothing runs unless the key
            is pressed.

endmenu
